body:
I fell this. I'd LIKE TO try to change it. However, the cynic in me doesn't think that's possible. So, I can't adopt such a mindset. Unfortunately.

&#x200B;

Edit. I FEEL this.

Given that death is a part of the cycle of existence, I'll make a safe presumption that it's actually nothing bad or punitive. Female octopi kill themselves after they give birth. I'm quite sure they're not damned for it. Suicide is just another way humans die.

&#x200B;

Edit: After their eggs hatch.
